{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794423639,"nonce":"qdAEhHLcgIny5PL/fkqUzTntkjE=","message":"hxcpp classes call their glue through an extern class since a92ae77.\n\n- `Hxn\u003cLibrary\u003eNative.hx` is one `extern class` a library: `@:include(\"\u003clibrary\u003e_glue.h\")`, the `@:buildXml` that used to sit on each interface's class, and one `@:native(\"\u003clibrary\u003e_glue::\u003cname\u003e\") static function \u003cname\u003e(...)` for every glue function. A handle is `cpp.RawPointer\u003ccpp.Void\u003e`, named `Handle` by a typedef private to that file.\n- The glue gained `release`, `memory_held` and `memory_wanted`, so nothing reaches past the namespace.\n- A null handle is `null` and is compared with `== null`; hxcpp's `null` converts to any pointer.\n- The typedef has to come before the metadata: with `@:buildXml` written above it the metadata attached to the typedef, the include path was never passed, and a clean build failed with \"'\u003clibrary\u003e_glue.h' file not found\". An incremental build over old objects did not show it.\n- A unit test holds every `Hxn\u003cLibrary\u003eNative.\u003cname\u003e` call to a declaration and every declaration to a glue function.\n\nRun from clean hxcpp output directories: tests/counter/run.sh gen-cpp and gen-emcc, tests/examples/run.sh cpp and emcc, tests/cli/run.sh cpp and emcc. HashLink output is unchanged.\n\nThe fixture's hand-written hxcpp classes under tests/counter/haxe/cpp still write C++ inline.","files":null}]}